WEBVTT

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:22.063
When a woman goes to Altair,
she either dies or becomes a man...

00:00:22.063 --> 00:00:23.857
Then, Mix, too?!

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:26.651
That wasn't the Mix we know.

00:00:26.651 --> 00:00:28.486
She had even lost her memory.

00:00:29.654 --> 00:00:32.073
Were you two okay, Zessica, Yunoha?

00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:34.159
We're okay now.

00:00:34.159 --> 00:00:37.328
Our medical checks showed no abnormalities,

00:00:37.328 --> 00:00:40.373
but if we had stayed there a bit longer,
we probably would've...

00:00:45.503 --> 00:00:47.589
So Mikono hasn't returned yet?

00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:51.009
She left to find Supreme Commander
Fudo and hasn't returned yet.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.179
How's Shrade doing?

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:58.308
He's no longer in critical condition,
but they said he needs bed rest.

00:00:58.308 --> 00:01:00.852
Damn it! The Supreme Commander is away.

00:01:00.852 --> 00:01:03.730
Shrade used up all his energy and is bedridden!

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.274
Isn't this the end for Neo-DEAVA?!

00:01:06.274 --> 00:01:08.234
Don't give up so easily!

00:01:09.819 --> 00:01:11.988
It's not over yet.

00:01:11.988 --> 00:01:15.867
We'll regroup and march into Altair once again!

00:01:15.867 --> 00:01:16.951
Andy...

00:01:16.951 --> 00:01:19.913
I'll rescue Mix! For sure!

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:26.378
Andy! Are you okay?

00:01:26.378 --> 00:01:28.046
I'm okay.

00:01:28.046 --> 00:01:30.382
I'm never gonna give up!

00:01:30.382 --> 00:01:36.054
I'll keep attacking them over
and over again until I get Mix back!

00:01:36.054 --> 00:01:40.558
<i>You're so beautiful it's depressing</i>

00:01:40.558 --> 00:01:48.608
<i>Let's love each other platonically</i>
<i>in this topsy-turvy world</i>

00:01:54.864 --> 00:02:05.250
<i>The world we're looking at</i>
<i>is always upside down</i>

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:14.217
<i>We don't have control</i>
<i>over how things get decided</i>

00:02:14.217 --> 00:02:19.848
<i>You're so hurt that your eyes are in tears</i>

00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:26.104
<i>I stayed silent while my heart cried out</i>

00:02:26.104 --> 00:02:38.199
<i>While the last two were kept apart,</i>
<i>the countdown has started</i>

00:02:38.199 --> 00:02:42.829
<i>You're so beautiful it's depressing</i>

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:48.710
<i>Let's love each other like animals</i>
<i>on the verge of extinction</i>

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:53.214
<i>You're so beautiful it makes me wanna cry</i>

00:02:53.214 --> 00:02:59.304
<i>I want to feel a platonic love</i>
<i>in this topsy-turvy world</i>

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:09.773
"Kiss"

00:03:09.773 --> 00:03:12.317
"Kiss"
I was so close...

00:03:12.317 --> 00:03:14.319
"Kiss"
I was just about to see it.

00:03:15.779 --> 00:03:20.450
The ultimate melody of love
played by the two worlds...

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:24.662
Don't talk any more.

00:03:24.662 --> 00:03:27.957
You need to focus on resting right now.

00:03:29.584 --> 00:03:35.173
I wonder if I can complete
the opus before my life ends...

00:03:37.092 --> 00:03:41.137
Would you tell me using
your Despair Prediction?

00:03:43.264 --> 00:03:46.142
Use my Despair Prediction?

00:03:46.142 --> 00:03:51.606
There are melodies that echo beautifully
precisely because of despair.

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:54.859
Shrade...

00:03:56.736 --> 00:04:02.867
Once my opus is completed, would you
play it with me, my good friend?

00:04:02.867 --> 00:04:06.538
Just when will Supreme
Commander Fudo come back?

00:04:06.538 --> 00:04:09.874
We haven't heard from Mikono at all, either.

00:04:09.874 --> 00:04:13.211
Would you like one, Miss Suomi?

00:04:13.211 --> 00:04:17.090
No, thank you. I try to avoid eating
high-calorie foods late at night.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.384
I see.

00:04:19.384 --> 00:04:22.303
There's no need to panic.

00:04:22.303 --> 00:04:27.934
Fudo will definitely come back...
with the myth of genesis.

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:35.734
You, the one with bright green hair...

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:44.701
It was unfortunate, wasn't it...? After I
opened the dimensional gate for you...

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:46.411
You are...

00:04:46.411 --> 00:04:47.912
No!

00:04:52.751 --> 00:04:55.086
I'll hold you to your promise.

00:04:55.086 --> 00:04:57.422
Promise?

00:04:57.422 --> 00:05:00.925
What did I promise...?

00:05:00.925 --> 00:05:04.179
You don't have to remember it yet.

00:05:04.179 --> 00:05:07.474
You'll fulfill your promise when the time comes.

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:24.491
Mix...

00:05:29.371 --> 00:05:34.793
Come to think of it, that means
that I saw her big bang...

00:05:34.793 --> 00:05:38.296
...though it wasn't a big bang at all.

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:42.676
Andy, what're you doing here?

00:05:42.676 --> 00:05:46.262
Unless I'm sitting here, I sink, so...

00:05:47.972 --> 00:05:51.768
That's one of the holes Mix filled...

00:05:51.768 --> 00:05:57.649
Yeah. There's no gap in the molecular
structure of the holes she filled.

00:05:57.649 --> 00:06:02.862
So even if my power gets out of control,
I won't find myself sinking.

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:06.825
Andy...

00:06:06.825 --> 00:06:09.202
Say, Amata...

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:14.082
Even if I get Mix back, will I be able to...

00:06:14.082 --> 00:06:17.168
Will I still be able to love...

00:06:17.168 --> 00:06:20.588
...Mix as a man the same way?

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:40.692
Oh, it's you... No wonder
I didn't smell anything.

00:06:45.572 --> 00:06:47.490
Stop it! Let go of me!

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:49.576
Why are you running away?!

00:06:54.664 --> 00:06:57.292
We've finally become one, huh?

00:06:57.292 --> 00:06:59.544
Apollon...

00:06:59.544 --> 00:07:01.796
I'm right here, Apollon.

00:07:04.549 --> 00:07:07.135
I was finally able to meet you.

00:07:07.135 --> 00:07:09.721
So you came to get me.

00:07:09.721 --> 00:07:11.056
Mikono!

00:07:11.056 --> 00:07:16.478
You damn woman.
We're not Apollon. We're Amagura!

00:07:20.899 --> 00:07:22.817
Wait, Mikono!

00:07:24.194 --> 00:07:26.237
Hold it, you damn woman!

00:07:30.784 --> 00:07:32.160
Stop it! Don't!

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:33.286
Shut up!

00:07:33.286 --> 00:07:36.373
You damn woman, I want you
to become one with us, too.

00:07:36.373 --> 00:07:39.459
No! Help!

00:07:39.459 --> 00:07:42.128
Amata! Stop it!

00:07:44.047 --> 00:07:46.591
Nooo!

00:07:56.643 --> 00:07:58.144
Mikono...

00:08:11.574 --> 00:08:13.118
Thank you.

00:08:15.662 --> 00:08:21.793
When you clap your hands together,
what exists in between?

00:08:21.793 --> 00:08:22.836
What?

00:08:22.836 --> 00:08:25.922
Your right hand and left hand.
Angels and humans.

00:08:25.922 --> 00:08:29.467
Man and woman. Yin and Yang.

00:08:29.467 --> 00:08:32.137
What is between them?

00:08:35.598 --> 00:08:38.810
Something that exists between
my right and left hands...?

00:08:46.109 --> 00:08:47.652
Darkness?

00:08:49.279 --> 00:08:51.489
There's nothing...

00:08:51.489 --> 00:08:53.199
...yet there's warmth.

00:08:55.493 --> 00:08:59.414
I feel like... I've heard this conversation before.

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:14.179
Once upon a time, shortly after
heaven and earth got separated,

00:09:14.179 --> 00:09:18.350
this world was filled with beautiful light.

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:24.189
Flowers sang, flying insects
and sacred beasts whispered love,

00:09:24.189 --> 00:09:29.152
and angels exchanged their love up in the stars.

00:09:29.152 --> 00:09:34.741
However, the terrifying thing was
that those angels would hunt humans.

00:09:36.868 --> 00:09:42.415
In the midst of battle, Apollonius,
who was known as the Massacring Angel,

00:09:42.415 --> 00:09:47.629
and a young woman named
Seliane met and fell in love.

00:09:49.881 --> 00:09:54.928
Apollonius betrayed his people
and sided with humans.

00:09:57.722 --> 00:10:01.601
Soon, the sinner Apollonius
abandoned his wings

00:10:01.601 --> 00:10:04.437
and fought alongside the
humans against the angels

00:10:04.437 --> 00:10:09.818
by operating the great power,
Mechanical Angel.

00:10:09.818 --> 00:10:13.905
This is the story written in
the Book of the Twin Stars.

00:10:13.905 --> 00:10:17.367
The truth about twelve thousand years ago?

00:10:17.367 --> 00:10:21.579
No, it goes back another cycle in time.

00:10:21.579 --> 00:10:25.083
This is a story from
twenty-four thousand years ago.

00:10:26.334 --> 00:10:29.546
And now fate has come full circle

00:10:29.546 --> 00:10:33.758
and a myth is about to be woven once again.

00:10:33.758 --> 00:10:36.678
A myth is... once again...

00:10:46.354 --> 00:10:48.982
Amata Sora! What do you think you're doing?!

00:10:48.982 --> 00:10:51.901
I don't remember giving
you the order to deploy!

00:10:51.901 --> 00:10:54.154
I'm gonna go look for Mikono!

00:10:54.154 --> 00:10:56.448
I won't allow disobedience!

00:10:56.448 --> 00:11:00.201
I feel like Mikono's calling me for help!

00:11:00.201 --> 00:11:02.454
So I have to go find her now.

00:11:12.505 --> 00:11:14.507
Mikono...

00:11:14.507 --> 00:11:17.886
I don't wanna see off someone
who's dear to me ever again.

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:26.644
Go to the one you love...

00:11:26.644 --> 00:11:30.899
...and to Solar Wing.

00:11:30.899 --> 00:11:36.363
You, other half... It's about time you awakened.

00:11:43.411 --> 00:11:45.080
Amata...

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:49.501
Vector Z's communication is shut off,
and so its location is unknown.

00:11:49.501 --> 00:11:53.421
Can you determine where Amata's
headed using your Despair Prediction?

00:11:53.421 --> 00:11:54.923
I'll try.

00:12:11.731 --> 00:12:13.233
This is...!

00:12:22.534 --> 00:12:25.120
The town where I met
Mikono for the first time...

00:12:28.707 --> 00:12:31.668
What on earth happened to it?

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:04.075
What is this place?

00:13:04.075 --> 00:13:06.619
As written in the Book of the Twin Stars,

00:13:06.619 --> 00:13:09.164
a place between the light and darkness.

00:13:12.167 --> 00:13:14.377
The cockpit is empty.

00:13:14.377 --> 00:13:15.962
That darn Amata!

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:20.091
The town where I encountered
Amata for the first time...

00:13:20.091 --> 00:13:23.887
...and where I merged
with him for the first time...

00:13:32.437 --> 00:13:33.980
No one's around...

00:13:35.648 --> 00:13:38.526
Where did everyone go?

00:13:40.445 --> 00:13:45.492
I heard that this town was specified
as an area under strict surveillance,

00:13:45.492 --> 00:13:47.744
but I never expected this.

00:13:47.744 --> 00:13:50.330
Is Mikono around here, too?

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:52.207
My Prediction is telling me so.

00:13:53.708 --> 00:13:57.712
As I thought... Amata went after Mikono.

00:13:57.712 --> 00:14:00.173
At any rate, let's split up and look for them.

00:14:10.809 --> 00:14:12.310
Pops...

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:42.841
Why are there so many pictures?!

00:14:42.841 --> 00:14:45.802
I didn't do this. Who on earth did it?!

00:14:48.847 --> 00:14:51.057
What's in this place?

00:14:51.057 --> 00:14:54.394
Why did Mykage tell me to come here?

00:14:55.937 --> 00:14:58.106
But this smell...

00:14:59.274 --> 00:15:01.026
It's no mistake.

00:15:01.026 --> 00:15:04.696
I've been to this town before, a long time ago.

00:15:27.635 --> 00:15:29.679
Amata...

00:15:29.679 --> 00:15:31.931
Amata...!

00:15:31.931 --> 00:15:33.433
Amata...

00:15:51.743 --> 00:15:56.998
Looks like... the seal on your
memory has finally been broken.

00:16:02.128 --> 00:16:04.673
"Skies of Aquaria"...

00:16:23.775 --> 00:16:25.276
Mikono...

00:16:30.699 --> 00:16:32.242
Mikono?!

00:16:38.957 --> 00:16:40.583
Amata!

00:16:40.583 --> 00:16:44.295
Zessica... What're you doing here?

00:16:44.295 --> 00:16:47.590
I came... after you.

00:16:50.593 --> 00:16:54.973
I came with Cayenne on Director Crea's orders.

00:16:54.973 --> 00:17:00.020
Ah... I'm sorry. I ignored her orders, so...

00:17:03.398 --> 00:17:06.943
I heard that this town is specified
as an area under strict surveillance

00:17:06.943 --> 00:17:09.237
and is now under an evacuation order.

00:17:09.237 --> 00:17:13.450
I see. That's why pops and the others are...

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:17.495
Why did you have to go so far as to
disobey orders to come to this town?

00:17:17.495 --> 00:17:20.206
I don't know... It's just...

00:17:20.206 --> 00:17:22.208
"It's just"...?

00:17:22.208 --> 00:17:24.961
I feel like Mikono is calling me.

00:17:30.091 --> 00:17:33.219
I will continue to wait for you...

00:17:33.219 --> 00:17:36.723
...even if I have to wait ten thousand
years and two thousand more.

00:17:43.355 --> 00:17:47.317
You used to work in this movie theater, right?

00:17:47.317 --> 00:17:51.154
And you met Mikono here.

00:17:51.154 --> 00:17:52.655
Zessica...

00:17:54.199 --> 00:17:56.034
Say, Amata...

00:17:56.034 --> 00:17:58.370
After...

00:17:58.370 --> 00:18:02.123
After another twelve thousand years...

00:18:02.123 --> 00:18:03.625
...will you...?

00:18:10.507 --> 00:18:16.304
We can do without fictional
stories created by human hands.

00:18:16.304 --> 00:18:21.226
A real myth will soon
return to life in this world.

00:18:25.230 --> 00:18:28.191
Zessica! Let's get out of here! This way!

00:18:29.901 --> 00:18:32.696
What're you doing?! Hurry!

00:18:32.696 --> 00:18:34.197
Yeah!

00:18:40.787 --> 00:18:45.875
Now, run, love beasts...

00:18:45.875 --> 00:18:48.128
...to the promised land.

00:19:02.058 --> 00:19:03.560
Amata!

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:08.481
Zessica!

00:19:11.735 --> 00:19:13.236
Zessica!

00:19:16.531 --> 00:19:17.782
Dammit!

00:19:17.782 --> 00:19:19.784
I can't! I can't slip out.

00:19:19.784 --> 00:19:21.536
Don't give up!

00:19:25.331 --> 00:19:28.418
Don't worry about me! Get out of here, Amata!

00:19:28.418 --> 00:19:33.381
No! I can't just leave you here!

00:19:33.381 --> 00:19:34.883
Amata...

00:19:41.014 --> 00:19:43.641
Thank you, Amata.

00:19:56.780 --> 00:19:58.865
No! Zessica!

00:20:08.416 --> 00:20:10.335
Zessica!

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:16.132
Amata! I've been looking all over for you!

00:20:32.357 --> 00:20:33.942
Sorry for keeping you waiting, Cayenne!

00:20:33.942 --> 00:20:35.402
Sazanka!

00:20:35.402 --> 00:20:37.904
Vector Y! Don't tell me...!

00:20:37.904 --> 00:20:43.535
You promised to play my final opus with me
once it's completed, right, good friend?

00:20:43.535 --> 00:20:46.996
Wait! If you merge in that
condition, your life will be...

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:53.086
We don't have time to hesitate! Let's go!

00:20:54.212 --> 00:20:58.425
Sutemi Gattai! Go! Aquarion!

00:21:02.762 --> 00:21:05.015
Shrade, you...

00:21:05.015 --> 00:21:07.058
Thank you, my good friend!

00:21:07.058 --> 00:21:10.103
Oh, I'm having naughty thoughts!

00:21:12.230 --> 00:21:14.899
Aquarion Spada!

00:21:29.497 --> 00:21:33.335
There you are... wimpy Amata!

00:21:34.919 --> 00:21:36.421
You...

00:21:43.219 --> 00:21:48.266
Solar Wing is now about to awaken.

00:21:48.266 --> 00:21:51.186
I have to apologize...

00:21:52.604 --> 00:21:56.691
I've been acting terrible. Please forgive me.

00:21:58.318 --> 00:22:00.111
You...

00:22:00.111 --> 00:22:02.864
Don't tell me what I saw that time was...

00:22:02.864 --> 00:22:06.493
Yeah, I thought it was an illusion or something.

00:22:25.595 --> 00:22:29.683
The wimpy Amata who ended up
not being able to do anything...

00:22:36.272 --> 00:22:38.066
So, as I thought, you are...

00:22:39.109 --> 00:22:40.610
That's right.

00:22:42.153 --> 00:22:44.447
My other half!

00:23:02.882 --> 00:23:10.807
<i>I saw a white flower on a slope</i>
<i>on my way towards you</i>

00:23:10.807 --> 00:23:18.440
<i>Even after awaking from my dream,</i>
<i>I gazed at a sad sky</i>

00:23:23.028 --> 00:23:28.825
<i>This feeling lives on a leaf's back</i>

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:38.251
<i>I listen closely to the sound </i>
<i>of the falling morning dew</i>

00:23:38.251 --> 00:23:46.051
<i>God, the world you created is not perfect</i>

00:23:46.051 --> 00:23:53.850
<i>Here, every day many loves fall and die</i>

00:23:53.850 --> 00:23:57.687
<i>This was my first time falling in love</i>

00:23:57.687 --> 00:24:00.982
<i>You don't even know it, do you...</i>

00:24:00.982 --> 00:24:05.445
<i>Even if you were on the other side of the earth,</i>

00:24:05.445 --> 00:24:08.656
<i>I wanted you to be by my side</i>

00:24:08.656 --> 00:24:13.119
<i>Even if you were going to forget about me,</i>

00:24:13.119 --> 00:24:19.209
<i>I wanted you to be by my side</i>

00:24:23.672 --> 00:24:27.592
Um, I think that Kagura
kinda has the wrong idea

00:24:27.592 --> 00:24:30.261
about how to deal with women.

00:24:30.261 --> 00:24:34.391
Love is rather a warm feeling, so...

00:24:34.391 --> 00:24:37.227
"Next Episode 'Wing’s Revival'"
Ah...!
